Description: tiling terminal emulator with split panes, tabs and broadcast
 SysTerm is a native GTK/VTE terminal in the spirit of Terminator: split the
 window into a tree of shell panes, arrange them in tabs, and broadcast your
 typing to every pane at once.
 .
 It is built on the VTE widget used by GNOME Terminal, so the terminal core
 (PTY, escape sequences, rendering, URLs, scrollback) is solid; SysTerm adds
 the tiling, tabs, broadcast input, a right-click context menu and a small
 config file for the profile and keybindings.
